{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Do not let your heads become disheveled.</b> Some say: to grow the side-locks." "<b>You shall not tear.</b> You shall tear. The correct view is that it is from בגדיו יהיו פרומים (his garments shall be torn) and his head shall be disheveled. The majority said: covered. Others said: uncovered. The truth is the words of tradition." "<b>And you shall not die.</b> The word ולא draws itself, like ולא למדתי חכמה (and I have not learned wisdom). So too it is ולא על כל העדה יקצוף (and on all the congregation he shall not be wrath), for you shall make atonement for them." "The sense of <b>and your brothers, all the house of Israel.</b> You will find it hinted at in the section of ראה אנכי."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:18.742934044Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}